# Using LLVM.org Clang compilers with libstdc++ and ABI compatibility [](https://docs.discoverer.bg/clang_pp_libstcpp_abi_compat.html#using-llvm-org-clang-compilers-with-libstdc-and-abi-compatibility)
## When Static Linking Works Across Different Standard Libraries [](https://docs.discoverer.bg/clang_pp_libstcpp_abi_compat.html#when-static-linking-works-across-different-standard-libraries)
### 1. No standard library types in public API [](https://docs.discoverer.bg/clang_pp_libstcpp_abi_compat.html#no-standard-library-types-in-public-api)
```
// Library compiled with libc++ (statically linked)
extern "C" {
    void* create_object(const char* name, int value);
    void destroy_object(void* obj);
    int get_value(void* obj);
}
```

## When static linking does not work across different standard libraries [](https://docs.discoverer.bg/clang_pp_libstcpp_abi_compat.html#when-static-linking-does-not-work-across-different-standard-libraries)
### 1. Standard library types in function return values [](https://docs.discoverer.bg/clang_pp_libstcpp_abi_compat.html#standard-library-types-in-function-return-values)
```
// Library compiled with libc++ (statically linked)
namespace testing {
    class Message {
    public:
        std::string GetString() const;  // Returns std::__1::string
    };
}
```

### 2. Standard Library Types in Function Parameters [](https://docs.discoverer.bg/clang_pp_libstcpp_abi_compat.html#standard-library-types-in-function-parameters)
```
nm library.so | grep "set_name" | c++filt
# Shows parameter type with std::__1:: namespace
```

### 3. Standard library types in public class members [](https://docs.discoverer.bg/clang_pp_libstcpp_abi_compat.html#standard-library-types-in-public-class-members)
```
Segmentation fault (core dumped)
# Or: std::bad_alloc, corrupted double-linked list, etc.
```

### 4. Exception Types Crossing Boundaries [](https://docs.discoverer.bg/clang_pp_libstcpp_abi_compat.html#exception-types-crossing-boundaries)
```
nm library.so | grep "runtime_error" | c++filt
# Shows exception types with std::__1:: namespace
```

### 5. Virtual function tables with standard library types [](https://docs.discoverer.bg/clang_pp_libstcpp_abi_compat.html#virtual-function-tables-with-standard-library-types)
```
// Library compiled with libc++ (statically linked)
class Base {
public:
    virtual std::string get_name() const = 0;  // Returns std::__1::string
    virtual void process(const std::vector<int>& data) = 0;  // Takes std::__1::vector&
};

class Derived : public Base {
public:
    std::string get_name() const override;  // Returns std::__1::string
    void process(const std::vector<int>& data) override;  // Takes std::__1::vector&
};
```

## Simple code examples [](https://docs.discoverer.bg/clang_pp_libstcpp_abi_compat.html#simple-code-examples)
### Example A: Library with C API (works) [](https://docs.discoverer.bg/clang_pp_libstcpp_abi_compat.html#example-a-library-with-c-api-works)
```
// library.cpp
#include <string>
#include <vector>

static std::vector<std::string> storage;  // Internal use of libc++

extern "C" {
    void* create_item(const char* name) {
        storage.push_back(std::string(name));  // Uses libc++ internally
        return reinterpret_cast<void*>(storage.size() - 1);
    }

    const char* get_item_name(void* item) {
        size_t index = reinterpret_cast<size_t>(item);
        return storage[index].c_str();
    }

    void destroy_item(void* item) {
        // Cleanup if needed
    }
}
```

### Example C: Library with opaque handle (works) [](https://docs.discoverer.bg/clang_pp_libstcpp_abi_compat.html#example-c-library-with-opaque-handle-works)
```
// library.cpp
#include "library.h"
#include <string>
#include <unordered_map>

static std::unordered_map<StringHandle, std::string> storage;  // Internal

StringHandle create_string(const char* value) {
    StringHandle h = new int(0);
    storage[h] = std::string(value);  // Uses libc++ internally
    return h;
}

const char* get_string_value(StringHandle h) {
    return storage[h].c_str();
}

void destroy_string(StringHandle h) {
    storage.erase(h);
    delete static_cast<int*>(h);
}
```
